# Superpowers: Spec-to-Code Workflow

Use this sequence for every non-trivial change.

## 1) Align Intent
- Read `.kiro/specs/*/requirements.md`, `design.md`, and `tasks.md` before coding.
- If implementation and specs diverge, update docs or call out the mismatch before/with code changes.

## 2) Implement in Vertical Slices
- Prefer small end-to-end slices over large refactors.
- For each slice: update models/contracts first, then core logic, then API/UI integration.

## 3) Preserve Contracts
- Keep API response shapes stable unless explicitly changing contract.
- If changing behavior, update both docs and tests in the same change.

## 4) Verification Gate
- Run or update unit/e2e tests that cover changed behavior.
- Validate critical paths: session start/progress/cancel/export and persistence.

## 5) Performance + Maintainability Check
- For hot-path changes, include a short runtime impact note.
- Prefer config flags and feature toggles for risky changes.
- Avoid introducing infra complexity unless there is measured need.

## 6) Done Criteria
- Code, tests, and docs are all updated.
- README and `.kiro` specs match current behavior.
- Any follow-up work is recorded in `tasks.md` with clear status.

